libri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:6pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:nonNumeric></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">21</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 15pt 0pt;"><a style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';" href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_ebsKqTBIDUWwO0wgeEaUmg_cont1" continuedAt="Tb_ebsKqTBIDUWwO0wgeEaUmg_cont2"><ix:continuation id="Tb_1_I-Ggvc80-BDplWX4YeNg_cont1"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;text-align:justify;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:13.7pt;padding:0pt;">*</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">The principal amounts outstanding are subject to variable interest rates, which are based on three-month SOFR plus fixed percentages. Therefore, the Company believes the carrying amount of these obligations approximates their fair value.</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;border:0;"><tr><td style="vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:13.5pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:0pt;text-align:justify;"><span style="font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;">**</span></p></td><td style="padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:0pt;text-align:justify;"><span style="font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;">The fair value was influenced by interest rates, the Company&#8217;s stock price and stock price volatility and was determined by prices observed in market trading. Since the market for trading of the 2026 Convertible Notes was not considered to be an active market, the estimated fair value was based on Level 2 inputs.</span></p></td></tr></table></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">2029 Term Loan </p><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On May 8, 2024, the Company entered into a senior secured term loan facility (the &#8220;2029 Term Loan&#8221;) and received p<span style="background:#ffffff;">roceeds, net of the original issuance discount, of </span><span style="background:#ffffff;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_tdqOe_f5-0CXD_azrlCFUA" contextRef="Duration_5_8_2024_To_5_8_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_TwoThousandTwentyNineTermLoansMember_Q9QG_sEuik-UdulLB-DJow" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromDebtNetOfIssuanceCosts" scale="6" id="Narr_JA-vyutSpEGLHjLrayHrcw">37.5</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> million. The net proceeds were used by the Company as part of the full repayment of the </span><span style="color:#212529;background:#ffffff;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_tdqOe_f5-0CXD_azrlCFUA" contextRef="As_Of_5_8_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_TermLoansMember_dcnrZIB6vUqFeGJ7MZr6Tw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFaceAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_vk6RrIh4xE-G6XxzSJ240w">250.0</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#212529;background:#ffffff;">&#160;million aggregate principal amount of&#160;</span><span style="background:#ffffff;">the senior secured term loan facility that the Company entered into on January 5, 2022 (as amended, the &#8220;2027 Term Loans&#8221;).</span><span style="color:#212529;background:#ffffff;">&#160;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The 2029 Term Loan matures on May 8, 2029 and accrues interest equal to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_KvWFLqLvJ0ylgVmvHJyZKQ" contextRef="As_Of_5_8_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_chrs_AnkuraTrustCompanyLlcMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_TwoThousandTwentyNineTermLoansMember__J4FzSI1Z0qGKeW91QLZTA" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_UQ_tUMAWqkiCbJpnbh5dmg">8.0</ix:nonFraction>%, plus a three-month SOFR rate per annum. The 2029 Term Loan provides for interest-only payments on a quarterly basis until maturity. <span style="background:#ffffff;">The loan agreement, by and among the Company, Ankura Trust Company, LLC and the lenders signatory thereto (the &#8220;2029 Loan Agreement&#8221;), contains certain covenants, and the Company was in full compliance with </span><span style="background:#ffffff;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_item_M7_je1Oex0ib1tUj8TtGxw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_TwoThousandTwentyNineTermLoansMember_ypcwWx0Jb0WVTyQ9Htq8fQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="chrs:NumberOfEventsInDefault" scale="0" id="Narr_1bWr4MBsTEeEOrS0bC93qA">no</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> events of default as of June 30, 2026.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Interest expense on the 2029 Term Loan was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_tdqOe_f5-0CXD_azrlCFUA" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_TwoThousandTwentyNineTermLoansMember_FOWyyncHtU6epMLP58oviQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:InterestExpenseDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_PbQe9i6yYUiHwu034EQN8w">1.2</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_tdqOe_f5-0CXD_azrlCFUA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_TwoThousandTwentyNineTermLoansMember_i-cYwiSv8USuQIh7CA30jg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:InterestExpenseDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_TKilZvgs5kG9EpSADbZf-A">2.4</ix:nonFraction> million for the three and six months ended June 30, 2026, and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_tdqOe_f5-0CXD_azrlCFUA" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_TwoThousandTwentyNineTermLoansMember_5nAMCPdd50KogOkdTiHu_Q" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:InterestExpenseDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_PjlBNlu5u0GSW8C-IhYWGQ">1.3</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_tdqOe_f5-0CXD_azrlCFUA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_TwoThousandTwentyNineTermLoansMember_lpTKihcrh0uGXQshcPg8Lg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:InterestExpenseDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_JOgkTBZjj0OAhw1YhZiqgA">2.6</ix:nonFraction> million for the three and six months ended June 30, 2025, respectively. </p><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Revenue Purchase and Sale Agreement<b style="color:#ff0000;font-weight:bold;"> </b></p><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="background:#ffffff;">On May 8, 2024, concurrent with the 2029 Term Loan, the Company entered into the Revenue Purchase and Sale Agreement with Coduet Royalty Holdings, LLC, as administrative agent, and the Purchaser Group. Under the terms of the Revenue Purchase and Sale Agreement, the Purchaser Group paid the Company </span><span style="background:#ffffff;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_tdqOe_f5-0CXD_azrlCFUA" contextRef="As_Of_5_8_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_RevenuePurchaseAndSaleAgreementMember_YD3ksV7aA0GLqzd2qANcCA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="chrs:RevenuePurchaseAndSaleAgreementPurchasePrice" scale="6" id="Narr_wvKxxZ-Ba0OZV2i73R1BqA">37.5</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> million, subject to certain conditions at closing (the &#8220;Revenue Purchase Price&#8221;). In exchange, the Company sold to the Purchaser Group a right to receive</span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_KvWFLqLvJ0ylgVmvHJyZKQ" contextRef="As_Of_5_8_2024_srt_ProductOrServiceAxis_chrs_UdenycaMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_RevenuePurchaseAndSaleAgreementMember_lsPJMoud3EiUMXqcpllz6g" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="chrs:RevenuePurchaseAndSaleAgreementRightToReceivePercent" scale="-2" id="Narr_oepoQ-vTVkqDUaEdL_X1dg">5.0</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> of U.S. net sales of UDENYCA and LOQTORZI with respect to a specified threshold applicable to UDENYCA net sales and a specified threshold applicable to LOQTORZI net sales during an applicable year and </span><span style="background:#ffffff;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_KvWFLqLvJ0ylgVmvHJyZKQ" contextRef="As_Of_5_8_2024_srt_ProductOrServiceAxis_chrs_UdenycaAndLoqtorziMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_RevenuePurchaseAndSaleAgreementMember_v18TMknlqUyt52EXDt8nJw" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="chrs:RevenuePurchaseAndSaleAgreementRightToReceivePercent" scale="-2" id="Narr_6g15_ef3P02GjccGgjviMA">0.5</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> of U.S. net sales of UDENYCA and LOQTORZI that exceeded the specified threshold during that year (the &#8220;Revenue Payment&#8221;) for each calendar quarter commencing May 8, 2024. The Purchaser Group&#8217;s right to receive the Revenue Payment terminates and the Company no longer has the obligation to pay Revenue Payments once the Purchaser Group receives the amount equal to </span><span style="background:#ffffff;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_KvWFLqLvJ0ylgVmvHJyZKQ" contextRef="As_Of_5_8_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_RevenuePurchaseAndSaleAgreementMember_YD3ksV7aA0GLqzd2qANcCA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="chrs:RevenuePurchaseAndSaleAgreementCertainConditionsPurchasePriceMultiplier" scale="0" id="Narr_La1zONkmCU2TqxLbbyQpgg">2.25</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> times the Revenue Purchase Price allocated to each product. The Company may also buy out the Purchaser Group&#8217;s rights to receive the Revenue Payments by triggering certain conditions and paying the Purchaser Group the unpaid portion of the </span><span style="background:#ffffff;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_KvWFLqLvJ0ylgVmvHJyZKQ" contextRef="As_Of_5_8_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_RevenuePurchaseAndSaleAgreementMember_YD3ksV7aA0GLqzd2qANcCA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="chrs:RevenuePurchaseAndSaleAgreementCertainConditionsPurchasePriceMultiplier" scale="0" id="Narr_JlOrN88INkiVynuyBPjh1g">2.25</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> multiple on the Revenue Purchase Price. The proceeds from the Revenue Purchase Price were used by the Company as part of the full repayment of the 2027 Term Loans. On April 15, 2025, the Company paid </span><span style="background:#ffffff;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_tdqOe_f5-0CXD_azrlCFUA" contextRef="Duration_4_15_2025_To_4_15_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_RevenuePurchaseAndSaleAgreementMember_us-gaap_IncomeStatementBalanceSheetAndAdditionalDisclosuresByDisposalGroupsIncludingDiscontinuedOperationsAxis_chrs_UdenycaBusinessMember_pOb9QAfOu0eETq7N0Gan1A" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="chrs:PaymentsToBuyOutRightToReceiveFuturePayments" scale="6" id="Narr_USc6UkyVaUSOo9SLml8P6A">47.7</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> million to buy out the Purchaser Group&#8217;s right to receive the Revenue Payments with respect to UDENYCA in accordance with the Revenue Purchase and Sale Agreement (the &#8220;UDENYCA Buy-out&#8221;).</span> </p><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="background:#ffffff;">The Revenue Purchase and Sale Agreement contains certain covenants, and the Company was in full compliance with the agreement as of June 30, 2026.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:24.5pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="background:#ffffff;">The </span>Revenue Purchase and Sale Agreement contains an embedded derivative that meets the criteria to be bifurcated and accounted <span style="background:#ffffff;">for as a freestanding instrument subject to derivative accounting. The allocation of the Revenue Purchase Price to the embedded derivative resulted in a </span><span style="background:#ffffff;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_tdqOe_f5-0CXD_azrlCFUA" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_RevenuePurchaseAndSaleAgreementMember_F21-WvPGWkOfcTAmRVwcug" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="chrs:DiscountOnRevenueParticipationLiabilityFromDerivativeInstrument" scale="6" id="Narr_qK0w84K-iEmN6M2JUUw3kQ">9.2</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> million discount on the revenue participation liability at inception. Additionally, there was </span><span style="background:#ffffff;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_tdqOe_f5-0CXD_azrlCFUA" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_chrs_RevenuePurchaseAndSaleAgreementMember_F21-WvPGWkOfcTAmRVwcug" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="chrs:IssuanceCostsOnRevenueParticipationLiability" scale="6" id="Narr_Yp1maB6pKkuQWRKX0FIHmA">1.4</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> million in issuance costs. The discount and issuance costs are amortized to interest expense over the estimated term of the Revenue Purchase and Sale Agreement using the effective interest method. In connection with the UDENYCA Buy-out, the unamortized portion of the discount and issuance costs related to UDENYCA was derecognized. The effective interest rate was </span><span style="background:#ffffff;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_KvWFLqLvJ0ylgVmvHJyZKQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_ProductOrServiceAxis_chrs_LoqtorziMember_0NNQjEHZqUKMSEJ_BR7w_A" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateEffectivePercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_B6L7hMUDuke0q_enDqaQfA">27.2</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> for the LOQTORZI portion at June 30, 2026. </span>For additional details on the Royalty Fee Derivative Liability, see Note 3. Fair Value Measurements.</p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">22</p></div></div>
